Rust rewrite surface audit (2026-09-27)

Production Java source files under hugegraph-store: 547
Rust source files in rewrite workspace (excluding target): 4 (three crates plus build script)

Representative Java surfaces still absent from Rust parity:
- HgStoreEngine: Raft RPC server, partition-engine lifecycle, PD synchronization and leader routing.
- PartitionInstructionProcessor: change-shard, split/move/clean partition instructions and Raft task submission.
- PartitionEngine / PartitionManager / ShardGroup: partition ownership, key-range metadata, replica membership and recovery.
- RaftOperation / RaftClosure: replicated command envelope and completion semantics.

Current Rust evidence covers durable atomic batches, qualified namespace isolation, network RPC contracts, restart recovery, and independent Oracle/differential traces. It does not prove Raft replication, partition movement, or Java end-to-end equivalence.

Selected next slice: define a minimal partition key-range/ownership state model in store-core and expose deterministic apply/restart tests before wiring transport or real Raft. Keep this separate from HGK1 key compatibility and preserve the raw-key unqualified scan rule.
